        <item>
            <title>0.89</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:32:24 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1791616991</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.89</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Onboarding has been redesigned as a full-window takeover with a step indicator, header and footer. It now includes in-app sign-in to your Addy account using an emailed one-time code.</li>
<li>Onboarding gained an Interface step, where you choose your layout, and a Project Import step. The import step discovers Git projects on your Mac so you can add them right away.</li>
<li>The Manual has been rebuilt with a hero page, illustrated scenes and topic pages. It has a searchable outline for jumping to any topic.</li>
<li>You can now select several worktrees at once in the sidebar and act on them in bulk.</li>
<li>The project header now stays pinned at the top of the sidebar while you scroll through worktrees.</li>
<li>A new Servers menu in the header shows the project&#x27;s servers through a pill button.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Servers now belong to the project rather than to individual panes, so they stay consistent as you move between panes and worktrees.</li>
<li>Telemetry batches are now attributed to the Addy account you&#x27;re signed in with.</li>
<li>Onboarding tool rows for GitHub, agent CLIs and your account have been refreshed. The Settings layout options now share the same layout picker views as onboarding.</li>
<li>Action buttons and the server footer bar now use a shared spinning-symbol indicator for in-progress states.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Internal Changes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Added tests for onboarding, email-code sign-in, telemetry, the Manual content, sidebar selection and the sticky header.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
